    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2NrsjZR67sYLkLtKqkMhftf)_\n\nStacked on #316 (base is its branch; retarget to `main` after #316 merges).\n\n## What\n- `sp-refile` no longer does `(require 'denote)`. That failure also stopped `sp-vulpea-ext` and `sp-org-ext`, which require it.\n- `sp-split--denote-rename` is replaced by `sp-split--file-by-tags`:\n  - asks for tags when the new note has none (`sp-split-ask-tags`, unchanged) and writes `#+filetags`;\n  - moves the file into the folder of its tags (`sp-notes-filing-folder`), keeping the name vulpea gave it;\n  - leaves it alone when it has no tags, is already there, or the target exists;\n  - then updates vulpea and `org-id` as before.\n- `sp-split--add-identifier` is removed (no more `#+identifier:`).\n- `sp-split-denote-names` becomes the obsolete alias of `sp-split-file-by-tags`.\n- Literate doc `sp-refile.org` updated (bullet lists); the two test files no longer stub `denote`.\n\n## Testing\n- New ERT test `sp-split-file-by-tags-moves-note-into-tag-folder` (vulpea stubbed); 12 tests in `sp-refile-test` and `sp-split-leave-parents-test` pass in batch Emacs 29.3.\n- Doc tangles to the same code as the committed `.el` (ignoring whitespace).\n- /untested/ with the real vulpea, the real vault and the GUI.\n- No CHANGELOG edit.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9hnWskPJso94gsTkL)_",
